course: dictionary
lesson: 13976
title: Lobed leaves and organs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lobe is a rounded part that sticks out from something. Your earlobe is a lobe, and so is each rounded part along the edge of an oak leaf. When something has lobes, we call it lobed. «The oak leaf was lobed, with rounded parts all along its edge.»
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. «The leaf had three lobes, so it was a three-lobed leaf.» Three lobes are three rounded parts, so three-lobed must mean having three rounded parts that stick out. Try your meaning in the sentence: the leaf had three rounded parts sticking out, and it still makes sense.
explain: In science, lobed can also describe the inside of the body. «The lungs are lobed, split into rounded sections.» Here lobed means divided into rounded sections. When you sort leaves in a nature study, you can group them as lobed, toothed or smooth-edged.
fact: Lobed means having lobes.
fact: A lobe is a rounded part that sticks out.
fact: «Oak leaves are lobed.»
fact: «Maple leaves are lobed too.»
fact: In science, «lobed» means divided into rounded sections, like a lung or the brain.
fact: «Deeply lobed» means the rounded parts reach far into the shape.
exercise: «The oak leaf was lobed, with rounded parts all along its edge.» What does lobed describe here? | How heavy the tree is | *The shape of the leaf | The sound the wind makes | The colour of the leaf
exercise: What is a lobe? | A sharp point | A dark, hollow hole | *A rounded part that sticks out | A flat, smooth surface
exercise: Sam sorts leaves into lobed, toothed and smooth-edged. Which leaf is lobed? | A leaf that is very tiny | A leaf with tiny sharp points along its edge | *A leaf with rounded parts sticking out along its edge | A leaf with a plain, unbroken edge
test: «The lungs are lobed.» In science, what does this mean? | The lungs are smooth and plain | *The lungs are divided into rounded sections | The lungs make a loud noise | The lungs are very small
test: «A three-lobed leaf has how many lobes?» | Four | Two | Five | *Three
exam: Which sentence uses lobed correctly? | The river was lobed and fast | The bell was lobed and loud | The sky was lobed and blue | *The oak leaf was lobed, with rounded parts sticking out
